# The inline declaration position accepts a stub body and nothing else. Folding the three inline
# fast paths into one classifying helper (#1238) widened it to every grouped spelling of `...` and
# to nothing more: a real expression on the declaration line is still rejected where it always was,
# at the first token after the `:`.
def f() -> int: 1 + 1


def main():
    print(f())
